WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.899 --> 00:00:06.840
Hello I'm Luis Bettenncourt. I'm the
director of the Global Sustainability

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.230
Summer School here at the Santa Fe
Institute. Today we're kicking off the

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:15.059
school. It will be two weeks which
students or lecturers will spend

00:00:15.059 --> 00:00:20.460
together trying to bring together in the
same place some of the state of the art in

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:25.580
thinking and in technology for how
cities are becoming more sustainable.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:30.000
Relative to previous schools we have a
much bigger emphasis on people, on

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.680
institutions, on new technologies that
are kind of bridging the human

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.840
experience with issues of the
environment: like mapping and evaluating

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:46.560
solar and wind potential of built spaces
and community organizations. And we are

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.520
also looking at many different places
and already at this stage many of their

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.800
implementation plans from Los Angeles to
Chicago to Santa Fe, from India to parts

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.410
of Asia and Africa.
it's an exciting world where we're seeing

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:03.270
change. We're seeing its complexity and
we're creating the knowledge that we

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:07.909
hope will make a difference in the
decades to come.

